# Render browser service settings. Read by carlos-emr-chromedriver.service.
#
# This file is 0640 root:carlos-render. It is NOT readable by the `carlos`
# account, and carlos.properties (0640 root:carlos) is not readable by
# carlos-render — the two principals deliberately cannot read each other's
# configuration, which is why the url-base below is delivered twice rather than
# shared through one file.
#
# CARLOS_RENDER_URL_BASE is a path prefix chromedriver serves its endpoints under.
# It raises the bar against blind local scanning, but it is NOT a boundary:
# systemd expands it into the process's argv, and /proc/<pid>/cmdline is
# world-readable, so any local uid that looks can read it. The control that
# actually bounds this port is that the browser runs as carlos-render, an account
# with no group and nothing worth taking.
#
# The service refuses to start if this is empty, because an empty --url-base makes
# chromedriver serve at the bare root — a downgrade with no error anywhere.
# Rotating it means updating eform_pdf_browser_service_url in carlos.properties to
# match and restarting both units.
CARLOS_RENDER_PORT=9515
CARLOS_RENDER_URL_BASE=
